ntent.com/u/2341755?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/martijnvm","html_url":"https://github.com/martijnvm","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martijnvm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martijnvm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martijnvm/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martijnvm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martijnvm/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martijnvm/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martijnvm/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martijnvm/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martijnvm/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2017-03-29T13:36:54Z","updated_at":"2017-03-29T13:44:49Z","body":"My Activity has a transparent window so basically when my video completes, I can see the content in the Activity behind it. That's my 'empty state' which I was referring too.\r\n\r\nThis is my piece of code:\r\n`videoView = new EMVideoView(getContext().getApplicationContext());`\r\n`videoView.setPreviewImage(previewBitmap);`\r\n`videoView.setVideoURI(getVideoUrl());`\r\n`videoView.setOnPreparedListener(this :: startVideo);`\r\n`addView(videoView, 0);`\r\n\r\nstartVideo just calls .start() on the videoView.\r\n\r\nI have double checked and my videos don't have empty frames at the end :).\r\n\r\nPS: Great reaction time! ","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/comments/290091851/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"martijnvm","id":2341755,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzNDE3NTU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2341755?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.g